  <name>Pawse</name>
  <summary>Fast native music player for your local library</summary>

  <developer id="io.github.popovpsk">
    <name>Aleksandr Popov</name>
  </developer>

  <description>
    <p>
      Pawse is a native music player for local libraries, built in Rust. It keeps a
      fluid 120+ fps interface and an untouched signal path, playing at your files'
      own sample rate and bit depth with a live bit-perfect indicator.
    </p>
    <p>Features:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Bit-perfect playback at the native sample rate</li>
      <li>Wide format support: FLAC, ALAC, MP3, WAV, OGG and DSD</li>
      <li>CUE sheets split single-file albums into tracks automatically</li>
      <li>Instant fuzzy search across albums, artists and tracks</li>
      <li>Time-synced lyrics from your files or fetched online</li>
      <li>Tag editor for single tracks or whole albums</li>
      <li>Remote control from any device on your network through a built-in web view</li>
      <li>System media controls and hardware media keys</li>
      <li>Over 20 built-in themes and 20 interface languages</li>
    </ul>
  </description>

  <launchable type="desktop-id">io.github.popovpsk.pawse.desktop</launchable>

